  "interpretation": "For this one authored rule, the global output directly reads an aggregate of all T SUnits while the scoped output reads an aggregate of N SUnits from its own sheet. The term_unit:NodesOfType counter measures only NodesOfType collection work; it omits Neighbours result cardinality, so its large global/scoped ratio is not a like-for-like total-work ratio. Total term evaluations and counter-off wall time are the more comparable measures here. Audit-on/off semantics match exactly. These current-host measurements on one controlled factor are not a natural-task scaling law.",
